[h1]FPS Map — Updated for 1.19 (Ironman & Multiplayer Safe)[/h1]

[b]A cleaner, crisper, lighter map — rebuilt from the ground up for Hearts of Iron IV 1.19.x and every DLC up to Thunder at Our Gates.[/b]

This is a maintained continuation of the much-loved [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2404689961]FPS Map by Mlecz[/url]. The original stopped receiving updates while the game kept changing under it — outdated shaders, missing arrow types and invalid textures caused crashes, invisible HQ lines and broken plan arrows. This version keeps the exact look you know and fixes everything underneath.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]✔ What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Non-reflective water[/b] — sky reflections removed; darker, calmer seas that make coastlines pop.
[*][b]Sharper, solid borders[/b] — country and state borders stay fully opaque when zoomed out.
[*][b]Calm close-up winter[/b] — snow, frost and snow on trees fade out as you zoom in, so the map no longer turns into a white sheet. The strategic view keeps vanilla winter, so you can still see where winter is. Rivers stay snow-free.
[*][b]Calmer fog of war up close[/b] — fog stays exactly where and as strong as in vanilla, but its glaring white wisps are a soft grey that drifts slower.
[*][b]Softer weather[/b] — snowfall, blizzards, rain and sandstorms at about a third of vanilla intensity, lightning glows instead of strobing, sea ice glares less. Weather sounds are unchanged.
[*][b]Clean, flat map arrows[/b] — unlit, unsaturated movement and battle-plan arrows with thinner bodies; no more neon blobs over the frontline.
[*][b]Coloured, readable icons[/b] — naval missions, air missions, plan buttons, top-bar and production bars.
[*][b]Lighter shader work[/b] — fully masked arrow pixels are discarded early and arrow/symbol lighting & fog passes are skipped.
[/list]

[h2]✔ Compatibility[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Game version[/th][td]1.19.x (tested on 1.19.4 "Operation Postern")[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]DLC[/th][td]Compatible with all DLC up to Thunder at Our Gates — every DLC arrow, symbol and effect definition of 1.19.4 is kept (checked file by file). In-game testing was done on the base game.[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]Ironman[/th][td]✔ Yes — achievements stay enabled[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]Multiplayer[/th][td]✔ Yes — no checksum change, no desync[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]Existing saves[/th][td]✔ Add or remove at any time[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]Millennium Dawn[/th][td]✔ Tested with 2.0.3 — load FPS Map [b]after[/b] Millennium Dawn[/td][/tr]
[tr][th]Total conversions[/th][td]Works with most; mods that replace [i]gfx/FX/maparrow.shader[/i] or [i]maparrows.txt[/i] should load [b]after[/b] this one[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Why is it Ironman & MP safe?[/b] The game checksum only covers [i]common/, events/, history/[/i] and map data files. This mod touches none of them — only shaders, textures and arrow visuals — so your checksum stays identical to vanilla and achievements remain available (verified in-game: the game checksum with FPS Map enabled is identical to the one without it).

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🛠 What was fixed compared to the original[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Crash / broken arrows fixed:[/b] the map-arrow shader was an outdated copy missing three effects the engine now requires (raid arrows, see-through plan arrows). Rebuilt from the 1.19 shader with the mod's style re-applied.
[*][b]HQ / general connection lines restored:[/b] 12 arrow and symbol types added in recent patches (deployed-general front lines, commander ability range, raid arrows) were missing and simply did not draw.
[*][b]Invalid reflection texture replaced:[/b] the water/sky reflection was a flat image where the game expects a cube map. Now a proper (black) cube map — same look, no rendering errors.
[*][b]Stretched UI bars fixed:[/b] deployment and fuel bars resized to the current UI slots.
[*][b]Smoother scaled icons:[/b] 10 map/UI icons now carry full mip chains like vanilla.
[*][b]Cleanup:[/b] 15 obsolete files removed (8 identical to vanilla, 7 that the game never loaded).
[/list]
Every changed file is rebuilt from the [i]current[/i] vanilla file with only the mod's own edits applied, so nothing new from Paradox is lost.

[hr][/hr]

