[hr][/hr]

[h2]📦 Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]In the Paradox Launcher, add [b]FPS Map - Updated for 1.19 (Ironman & MP Safe)[/b] to your playset.
[*][b]Disable the original FPS Map[/b] if you have it — both replace the same files.
[/olist]

[h2]❓ FAQ[/h2]
[b]Will it really raise my FPS?[/b]
It removes some per-pixel work from water, rivers and arrows. The gain depends on your GPU and zoom level; it shines most on mid-range and laptop GPUs during large wars with many plan arrows. It will not fix CPU-bound late-game slowdowns — that is the game simulation, not the map.

[b]Does it change gameplay?[/b]
No. Purely visual.

[b]Can I use it with other UI / map mods?[/b]
Yes, unless they replace the same files (listed above). Put the mod you want to win lower in the load order.

[b]Sea and land regions show names like "STRATEGICREGION_49" — is this mod broken?[/b]
No — FPS Map ships no text at all. This happens when the game's debug-mode map editor (Nudger) leaves files in your user folder, which override every mod. Go to [i]Documents/Paradox Interactive/Hearts of Iron IV/[/i] and move the [i]localisation[/i] and [i]map[/i] folders' contents somewhere else (keep a copy). The broken file is usually [i]localisation/english/strategic_region_names_l_english.yml[/i] with lines like [i]KEY:-1 "..."[/i]; a leftover [i]map/unitstacks.txt[/i] also changes your checksum and can block Ironman achievements.

